WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:10.769
"Is Water Fluoridation Safe?"

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.340
Fluoride&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.100
had been found to be
a developmental neurotoxin

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.060
in rats and mice,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:16.860
leading to learning
and memory deficits,

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.320
which led to an interest
in studying human populations.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.480
Starting in the 1980s,

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.760
reports started appearing
in Chinese medical journals

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.560
that found correlations
between areas

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.840
naturally containing higher
fluoride levels in water

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.240
with lower intelligence
among children.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.500
Dental fluorosis, the
fluoride-induced tooth mottling,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.700
is widespread in China,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.400
with more than
90 million residents affected,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.860
often in small pockets
surrounding particular

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.780
small springs
or mountain sources.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.880
Researchers took
advantage of the fact

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.400
that even adjoining
neighborhoods could have

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.620
wildly different
fluoride exposure,

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.900
setting up a type
of natural experiment.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.680
Due to limited access
to Chinese journals at the time,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.900
these studies largely
escaped the attention

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:58.980
of scientists in the West

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.100
until a meta-analysis
of 16 such studies

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.860
was published in English
in 2008.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.520
"Fluoride and Children's
Intelligence: A Meta-analysis"

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:11.760
found that children living
in areas prone to fluorosis

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.180
had five times higher odds
of developing low IQ

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.180
than those living in areas
with little or no fluorosis.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.200
So, here we were,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.200
thinking dental fluorosis
was just a cosmetic blemish,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.780
but it may instead
be a visual indicator

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.580
of intellectual deficits.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.400
A subsequent
meta-analysis in 2012

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.080
including about 10 more studies

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:33.360
found that the average
intelligence gap between

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.320
high and low fluoride exposure
areas was about seven IQ points.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.620
By far the largest study,
involving thousands of children,

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:44.220
it found that even
at fluoride levels below 1 ppm,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.560
higher fluoride levels
were associated with

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.720
a large drop
in the chances of developing

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.860
excellent intelligence,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.320
defined as an IQ
of 130 or higher.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.640
Even very mild fluorosis was
associated with less than half

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.860
the odds of reaching
such a high IQ.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.240
By now, there have been
more than 50 studies showing

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.240
an association between higher
fluoride exposure and lower IQ.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:09.060
In the latest systematic
review meta-analysis,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.640
90 percent of the studies
published in the last ten years

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.960
reported a link between

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:15.360
high fluoride exposure
and reduced intelligence.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.440
However, serious caveats
are in order.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:22.140
First, the fluoride
concentrations

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:23.220
in most of these studies

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.200
were well above
fluoridation levels.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.320
In the 2012 meta-analysis,
for example, one study clocked

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.620
concentrations
as high as 11.5 ppm,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.520
far exceeding the US target
of 0.7 parts per million

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.500
as well as
the average concentration

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.160
in the United States,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.520
which is around 0.8 ppm
in municipal water

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.680
and 0.3 ppm in well water.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.020
Now, to be fair,

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:49.380
the 11.5 ppm in the
meta-analysis was an outlier.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.600
The average elevated level
was only about

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.740
two parts per million,

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.200
and most found
associated IQ decrements

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.240
below the EPA's upper limit,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:00.360
its Maximum Contaminant Level
Goal of four ppm,

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.520
which is supposed
to represent the level

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.580
"below which there is no known
or expected risk to health."

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.580
Some studies showed
lower intelligence

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.880
with fluoride concentrations
even down at one to two ppm

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.260
with one estimate suggesting

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.480
the smallest harmful
concentration,

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.760
potentially shaving off
a single IQ point,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.940
would be down around 0.3 ppm,

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.980
assuming you drink
four cups of water a day,

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:25.680
while others suggest
it's too early to be able

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.380
to calculate a threshold
for human neurotoxicity

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.720
due to insufficient
available data.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.740
The second major caveat
is confounding.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.260
Nearly all of the studies
to date have been performed

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.180
in rural communities
in countries like China,

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.560
Iran, and Mongolia.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.360
Areas within these countries

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.160
with unusually high
fluoride levels

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.560
may be particularly
poor and underdeveloped,

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.360
since relatively
rich communities

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.300
may be more likely to invest
in higher-quality drinking water

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.620
that filters out fluoride,

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.780
if only to reduce
dental fluorosis.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:58.500
High fluoride water may also be
more likely to be contaminated

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.360
with other neurotoxins.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.500
Fluoride exists in water as
a negatively charged particle.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.900
To maintain electroneutrality,

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.880
this may pull
into the groundwater

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:11.040
positively charged particles
such as aluminum,

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.660
arsenic, lead, or mercury.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.540
This doesn't happen
in community water fluoridation

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.360
since the negative fluoride ions
are balanced out

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.860
in the water treatment process.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.740
Finally,
most of the older studies

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.720
were cross-sectional
and ecological,

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.240
meaning they looked
at a snapshot-in-time

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.560
of group level data rather than
individual-exposures-over-time.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.120
Just because a child with low IQ
lives in a high fluoride area

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.640
doesn't necessarily mean
they or their mom actually

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.260
drank the water, for example.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:44.280
Ideally, we'd be able to measure
individual exposure levels

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.140
and then follow
the kids over time

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.000
to see if those
with higher exposure

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.340
really do grow up
with stunted intellects,

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.340
and that's exactly what
we'll cover in my next video,

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:58.080
entitled "Why I Changed My Mind
on Water Fluoridation."

